# plan__ta-veto-liveness-round2-done

Round-2 follow-ups for PR D (#1481, ta-veto-liveness) are implemented, committed, and green.
Branch was first rebased onto current upstream/main, then the three folds + dev-guide update landed.

## State
- Branch `ta-veto-liveness`, tip `5d324b36`. Rebased onto upstream/main `dfc21e2c`.
- 8 commits from base (6 round-1 + 2 round-2). DCO 8/8.
- **NOT pushed** — #1481 is OPEN; Dean force-pushes with `--force-with-lease` when ready.
- All gates green: gofmt clean, `go build ./...`, `go vet`, `make test` (no failures),
  `make lint` (0 issues), `-race` on pipeline+saturation_v2+saturation.

## What changed (round-2)
Two commits:

1. `61060530` — **D.1** single source of truth for the no-data/error reason sentinels.
   Promoted to exported `pipeline.ReasonNoData` / `pipeline.ReasonError`; saturation_v2 aliases
   the shared const and returns `pipeline.ReasonError` instead of literals. Decision was PROMOTE
   (no pin test) after confirming no import cycle. The `"no-data"`/`"error"` literals in
   saturation_v2 are DEPRECATED/removed, superseded by the shared constants.

2. `5d324b36` — **D.2** prune `lastGoodAnalysis` of departed models (selective eviction in
   `optimizeV2`, keyed identically to the liveness map, empty-set guarded) + **D.3** warn-only
   demand-liveness detector (`detectDemandLiveness` in `updateLivenessAndSetLive`; NUL-delimited
   synthetic demand-latch key; timestamp-gap signal seeded on first live supply so cold-start does
   not false-positive; never sets Live / touches RoleSpare / gates a decision) + engine-level test
   (4 cases, all pass) + dev-guide round-2 paragraph.

## DEFERRED (recorded in code comment + status file)
Per-pod demand latch: when demand becomes per-replica, the demand-latch key extends with a pod
component (`"\x00" + podID`) and a per-replica latch is tracked alongside the model-level one. Not
built — 0.9 demand is model-level only.

